# Othergame, built by the makefile beside this one.
#
#     wmake -f Makefile.othergame          the exe
#     wmake -f Makefile.othergame data     fonts, cutscenes and other.pak
#
# This was a whole copy of Makefile once, and the copies drifted: all three
# per-game files still said `TARGET = miwa.exe` and `PAK = miwa.pak` long
# after Makefile moved to mrpy.*, so building any game's data wrote a pak
# named for a different one. GAME and PAK are the only things that ever
# differed, so they are all that is left here; the flags, the object list,
# the header stamp, the libraries and every target come from Makefile, and a
# change there now reaches all four games.
#
# TARGET is deliberately not set: the exe is byte-identical whichever game
# it is shipped with -- only mrpy.rc's version block differs, and that is
# shipped per game -- so every build is mrpy.exe.
#
# Makefile sets each of these only `!ifndef`, so these win. A command-line
# macro -- `wmake -f Makefile.othergame PAK=other.pak` -- still beats both.

GAME = ../othergame/game
PAK  = other.pak

!include Makefile
